  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tien Len. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Tien Len (Tiáº¿n LÃªn), often called 'Thirteen' or 'Killer 13', is the national card game of Vietnam. It is a climbing/shedding game similar to Big Two and President. Players race to empty their hands by playing combinations that beat the previous play. The Two (Heo) is the highest card, and special 'bombs' can beat Twos.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to shed all cards from your hand; the last player left holding any cards loses the game.',
    gameplay: "First round: Player with 3 Spades starts. Subsequent: Winner of last round starts. Play combination (Single, Pair, Triple, Run). Next player must beat it with same type and higher rank/suit. Pass = out for the trick. 2s are high. 'Bombs' (4-of-a-kind, double runs) can beat 2s out of turn (Chopping). Winner is first out. Others play for 2nd, etc., or game ends.",
    keyRules: [
      '2 is highest',
      'Suit rank matters (Hearts highest)',
      'Chopping (Bombs beat 2s)',
      'Must beat with same number of cards (usually)',
    ],
